<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wilusa</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Wilusiya</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wilusa was a land in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> named in Hittite texts of the late <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bronze-age">Bronze Age</a>, appearing as Wilusiya in the record of the Assuwa coalition. A treaty of about 1280 BCE binds its king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alaksandu">Alaksandu</a> to the Hittite king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muwatalli-ii">Muwatalli II</a>. Many scholars identify it with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/troy">Troy</a>, Greek Wilios or Ilios, though the link remains debated.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wilusa.jpg" alt="Wilusa" width="320" height="197" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Al-qamar · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hethiter.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
